  "id": "b1-larret-qui-a-change-le-trajet",
  "title": "L'arrêt qui a changé le trajet",
  "titleEn": "The stop that changed the trip",
  "level": "B1",
  "minutes": 6,
  "summary": "Residents compare the effects of a temporary route change and decide what information to send back.",
  "unit": "b1-u06",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "fr": "Pendant les travaux, l'autobus ne passait plus devant le centre communautaire.",
      "en": "During construction, the bus no longer passed in front of the community centre."
    },
    {
      "fr": "L'arrêt temporaire se trouvait près d'une entrée accessible, mais le détour allongeait le trajet de plusieurs résidents.",
      "en": "The temporary stop was near an accessible entrance, but the detour lengthened several residents' trips."
    },
    {
      "fr": "Mina, qui travaillait tôt, arrivait encore à l'heure en partant dix minutes plus tôt.",
      "en": "Mina, who started work early, could still arrive on time by leaving ten minutes earlier."
    },
    {
      "fr": "Son voisin, qui accompagnait sa mère au centre, disait que le détour était plus difficile avec un fauteuil roulant.",
      "en": "Her neighbour, who accompanied his mother to the centre, said the detour was harder with a wheelchair."
    },
    {
      "fr": "Le comité a donc demandé où se trouvait la rampe et combien de temps les travaux dureraient.",
      "en": "The committee therefore asked where the ramp was and how long construction would last."
    },
    {
      "fr": "La ville a répondu que l'accès serait vérifié chaque semaine et que l'arrêt reviendrait après les travaux.",
      "en": "The city replied that access would be checked each week and the stop would return after construction."
    },
    {
      "fr": "Les résidents ont envoyé leurs observations, sans conclure qu'un trajet convenait à tout le monde.",
      "en": "Residents sent their observations without concluding that one route suited everyone.",
      "note": "A change can help one group and create difficulty for another; a useful report names both effects."
    }
  ],
